ers. I will justify why such blame is not justified and I deny any responsi=
bility for the respondent's insubordination in its entirety. I further take=
 offense to such blame and consider such conduct unwarranted, unjustified a=
nd harassment.

The respondent attached my list of documents that I found them to be missin=
g, had the respondent complied with court orders, such effort and document =
would not have been necessary. Had the respondent provided evidence in a ti=
mely manner rather than 24 minutes before deadline, such efforts by myself =
could have been highlighted and resolved earlier. Therefore, I wholly rejec=
t the implication of the timing of my document to be any cause of the delay=
s by the respondent. The delay are entirely at fault of the respondent and =
I will further elaborate.

The respondent conduct is extremely prejudicial to my claim. I will elabora=
te further as to why including some of the laws I seek to rely on.

The respondent's reference to when the witness statements are due is inappr=
opriate and seeks to deflect attention from their multiple insubordinations=
 of the courts, particular order 3.1 and 4.1. I will evidence as such.



I will also clarify why I cannot work with the respondent or their represen=
tative in the matters of this case as they have betrayed the trust the cour=
t, the SRA, wider society and I have placed on them.

As a preview to my document, I will be evidencing why the respondent and th=
eir representative's conduct justifies a default order win in my favour as =
the claimant.



The respondent states their requested orders are justified to save the cour=
t time and money. I will explain why their conduct and actions up until thi=
s point suggests the later and that the court should not justify their exte=
nsion to make up for their insubordination. My suggestion in my document wi=
ll be more appropriate than the respondent's suggestion of an extension.



Kind regards,

Abdul Alim



