<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">Dear Courts,</span><o:p></o=
:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p=
>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">I request the court reject =
this notion in its entirety. I will be submitting a request to the court to=
day and I am hoping for this to be issued before 5pm. Therefore, before rec=
eipt of this document, I wish for
 the court to wait this request to be received and to be considered in full=
.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p=
>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent and their re=
presentatives have acted in bad faith which I will further elaborate.</span=
><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent seeks to bla=
me me for their failure to comply with court orders. I will justify why suc=
h blame is not justified and I deny any responsibility for the respondent's=
 insubordination in its entirety.
 I further take offense to such blame and consider such conduct unwarranted=
, unjustified and harassment.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent attached my =
list of documents that I found them to be missing, had the respondent compl=
ied with court orders, such effort and document would not have been necessa=
ry. Had the respondent provided evidence
 in a timely manner rather than 24 minutes before deadline, such efforts by=
 myself could have been highlighted and resolved earlier. Therefore, I whol=
ly reject the implication of the timing of my document to be any cause of t=
he delays by the respondent. The
 delay are entirely at fault of the respondent and I will further elaborate=
.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent conduct is e=
xtremely prejudicial to my claim. I will elaborate further as to why includ=
ing some of the laws I seek to rely on.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent's reference =
to when the witness statements are due is inappropriate and seeks to deflec=
t attention from their multiple insubordinations of the courts, particular =
order 3.1 and 4.1. I will evidence
 as such.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p=
>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">I will also clarify why I c=
annot work with the respondent or their representative in the matters of th=
is case as they have betrayed the trust the court, the SRA, wider society a=
nd I have placed on them.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">As a preview to my document=
, I will be evidencing why the respondent and their representative's conduc=
t justifies a default order win in my favour as the claimant.</span><o:p></=
o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p=
>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">The respondent states their=
 requested orders are justified to save the court time and money. I will ex=
plain why their conduct and actions up until this point suggests the later =
and that the court should not justify
 their extension to make up for their insubordination. My suggestion in my =
document will be more appropriate than the respondent's suggestion of an ex=
tension.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p=
>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">Kind regards,</span><o:p></=
o:p></p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">Abdul Alim</span><o:p></o:p=
></p>
